{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfiGngLti8Epdiiat88Bk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The self-check passed (`OK`). Candidate 4 is in `experiment2/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_4/`.\n\n**Model name:** `person_specific_chance_switch_belief`\n\n**What it refines:** the incumbent, `length_normalised_chance_vs_motif`. Everything else is kept as it was: the fair coin compared against three regular generators (a switch-biased coin, a biased coin and a repeating motif with slips), the evidence divided by a fitted power of sequence length, and each person's own decision sensitivity.\n\n**The one change:** each person has their own belief about how often a fair coin switches, drawn from a population distribution. In the incumbent everyone shares one over-alternating belief. With this change, most people can still expect chance to switch often while some believe a fair coin is streaky and so pick the sequence with fewer switches. This targets the critique's one finding that survives the multiple-comparison correction: 18.8% of participants prefer fewer-switch sequences, where the incumbent predicts about 5%. The incumbent can't produce that, because its sensitivity can only be positive and its belief about chance is shared.\n\n**Self-check results:**\n- It loads, its log-probability is finite and it meets the data contract.\n- The 100-draw smoke fit gave a finite ELPD-LOO of −2109.2. That number comes from a single short chain, so it can't be fairly compared with the incumbent's −2318.3.\n\n**Risks at admission:**\n- **Speed:** the 200-iteration smoke fit took 251 seconds. A full production fit may come close to the 30-minute limit per sampling run.\n- **Reliability of the score:** 7.2% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5, so the score was flagged as unreliable. That is expected with 400 extra per-person parameters, but if the full fit stays above the 1% tolerance, the model can't be exported as the winner.\n- **Not yet checked:** convergence (the check uses one chain, so there is no R-hat) and novelty against the other models."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4386,"cache_read_input_tokens":68465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4386,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eb7b642-a4d9-489c-8290-3d792e8d28e9","uuid":"922e5189-6feb-4493-a01d-31f005562555","timestamp":"2026-10-05T02:06:57.724Z","request_id":"req_011CfiGnfS5juBgk6nm1F3Dv"}
